      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Best effort per orchestrator instruction: 'ñɩɣyʊʊ {h}' (ñɩɣyʊʊ = hour, numeral follows noun) + additive 'nɛ miniti N' (nɛ = and, miniti = minute loan), 'nɛ hɔɔlʊʊ' (half) at 30. Doubts: (1) tens numerals nɩɩlɛ 20 / niidozo 30 / nɩɩnaza 40 / nɩɩnʊwa 50 are from memory and 50 in particular is unverified; (2) whether Kabiye speakers say clock time with ñɩɣyʊʊ + bare numeral or a different idiom (many would say it in French); (3) existing hour names 'naanaza' (4; standard 'naanza') and 'lɛɛtɛ' (8; standard 'lutozo') look doubtful but were left as is. Needs a Kabiye speaker."
